# Time: seed the time_daemon offsets in /data from the persist partition.
#
# time_daemon (stock vendor) keeps the RTC-to-time offsets in
# /data/vendor/time/ats_<base>. Base 1 (time of day) is only updated through
# the stock system's time hooks, which 18.1 does not have, so after a
# userdata wipe the file never appears. time_daemon then resets the offset to
# a hardcoded 2018-01-01 08:59:35 UTC, and the clock stays wrong until NITZ or
# NTP corrects it. The stock firmware left valid offsets on persist.
#
# Copy them once per userdata (init cannot test for a file, so a persistent
# property marks it done). zygote-start runs after persistent properties are
# loaded and before class main (time_daemon) starts. If persist has no
# offsets, the copies fail harmlessly and NITZ/NTP sets the time as before.
on zygote-start && property:persist.hlte730t.time_seeded=""
    mkdir /data/vendor/time 0700 system system
    copy /mnt/vendor/persist/time/ats_1 /data/vendor/time/ats_1
    copy /mnt/vendor/persist/time/ats_2 /data/vendor/time/ats_2
    copy /mnt/vendor/persist/time/ats_16 /data/vendor/time/ats_16
    chown system system /data/vendor/time/ats_1
    chown system system /data/vendor/time/ats_2
    chown system system /data/vendor/time/ats_16
    chmod 0600 /data/vendor/time/ats_1
    chmod 0600 /data/vendor/time/ats_2
    chmod 0600 /data/vendor/time/ats_16
    restorecon_recursive /data/vendor/time
    setprop persist.hlte730t.time_seeded 1
